O(n² √m).","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","title":"DirectedGraph","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/minimumCostFlow(supply:capacity:cost:)":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A least-cost flow meeting every supply (positive: the vertex sends that much more than it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"receives; negative: a demand), within capacities (LEMON "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NetworkSimplex"},{"type":"text","text":", OR-Tools"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SimpleMinCostFlow"},{"type":"text","text":", NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"min_cost_flow"},{"type":"text","text":" with the opposite sign), or nil when there is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"none: the supplies do not sum to zero, or some set of vertices supplies more than its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out-edges carry. Costs may be negative; negative cycles are saturated (capacities are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"finite). A self-loop carries its capacity when its cost is negative and nothing otherwise."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Network simplex with block-search pivots and strongly feasible trees, LEMON’s layout."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"supply"},{"type":"text","text":" is called once per vertex in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, then, for each edge in position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" and then "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cost"},{"type":"text","text":", before any work. Which optimum is returned when several"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exist is unspecified, but the same input always gives the same result."}],"type":"topic","title":"minimumCostFlow(supply:capacity:cost:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/minimumCostFlow(supply:capacity:cost:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/flows\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/minimumcostflow(supply:capacity:cost:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumCostFlow"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"supply"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"capacity"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"co